WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.786
"How to Get Rid of Garlic Breath"

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.720
Approximately
one in three people

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:11.880
suffer from halitosis-
bad breath.

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:14.000
What can we do about it?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.480
I've got videos
on tongue cleaning, gum chewing,

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.120
and the best mouthwash.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.920
Population studies suggest
that those who eat

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.900
fewer fruits and vegetables
may be at higher risk,

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.680
but there are a lot of things
associated with worse diets

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:28.760
that are also linked
to halitosis,

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:29.800
though the fruit
and vegetable link

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.760
seemed to remain
even after controlling

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.000
for these other factors.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.840
It works in dogs.

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.080
Vegetable chew toys
seem to help,

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.920
but what about people?

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:41.960
There's a compound found
in cruciferous vegetables

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:45.240
that can effectively eliminate
the volatile sulfur compounds

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.680
like the rotten egg gas
hydrogen sulfide.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.440
These are the foul gases
that cause bad breath

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:51.920
produced mainly
from the breakdown

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.560
of sulfur-containing
amino acids

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:57.880
concentrated in animal protein-
cysteine and methionine.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:01.320
The cruciferous compound gloms
onto the sulfur compound

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.440
and prevents it
from going gaseous;

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:05.520
whereas peppermint,
spearmint, wintergreen,

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:08.160
and many of the flavors
in breath mints and chewing gum

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.680
didn't actually treat the cause,

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.080
and just kind of have
a masking effect.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.040
Whereas something
like broccoli chewing gum

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.000
might help
at least temporarily,

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.440
but why not just eat broccoli
instead?

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.240
Researchers have tried
using a compound

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.160
that clears cysteine
from the tongue

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:27.360
for those who don't just want
to try to cut down on casein

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.960
and other animal proteins
that are concentrated in it.

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.640
The compound they used
is derived from kiwi fruit,

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.600
so can you just eat kiwis
instead?

00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:36.840
No word on halitosis,

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.480
but twice daily kiwi fruit
consumption for two months

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:42.880
showed significant improvements
in gingivitis, plaque,

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.320
and gum disease.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:47.200
Of course, not all fruits
are going to be beneficial.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.200
Durian fruit may give rise
to the most profound bad breath

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.480
because the fruit itself
stinks to high heaven,

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.720
as many of you will remember

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.800
from my harrowing experience
with it in medical school

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.680
that I sheepishly related
in my book How Not to Die.

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:04.800
And the vegetable
that comes to mind

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:08.520
when you think bad breath
is garlic.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.040
Is there anything you can do
to deodorize garlic breath

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:14.400
using different kinds of foods?

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.920
Well, you don't know
until you put it to the test.

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.600
After giving people
some garlic,

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:23.160
they tried whey protein,
lemon juice, green tea,

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:26.080
chlorophyll, 7UP soda,
a raw pink lady apple,

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:29.320
a cooked apple, parsley,
spinach, and mint leaves.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:34.720
Anyone want to take a guess
as to which worked best?

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.640
Parsley, spinach,
and mint treatments

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.720
were effective
in the deodorization

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.800
of garlic breath
stinky compounds.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:45.360
They're all green,
so they wondered

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.720
if it was the chlorophyll,
and it turned out, nope,

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:49.840
chlorophyll alone didn't help.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.360
Here are the graphs.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.680
There are four
stinky garlic compounds.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:55.560
If you don't do anything
after the garlic,

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.840
the stench goes away
on its own.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.880
And taking chlorophyll didn't
seem to change that at all,

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:03.640
but parsley, spinach,
and mint did,

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:06.600
starting almost immediately.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.560
What do we think was going on?

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.040
Well, raw apples worked better
than cooked apples,

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.960
which are basically
the same food

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.880
except for the enzymes
being destroyed by heating,

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:19.320
so maybe there's
some enzymatic deodorization.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:20.640
Here's the data.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.440
And, yes, raw worked better
than cooked,

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.400
but cooked still worked
better than nothing,

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.640
and so did the lemon juice
and green tea,

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.520
even though they didn't have
any active enzymes

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:33.200
since they were
both pasteurized.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.160
Here's the beverages data.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.960
The whey protein in water
didn't seem to help at all,

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.080
even compared with the soda,

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.600
though green tea and lemon
appeared to do better.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:45.720
Maybe the acidic pH

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.360
was involved
in the deodorization

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.120
from the lemon juice

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.000
and soft drink
breath experiments,

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:54.040
since they used
a sour lemon-lime soft drink.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:57.840
Garlic breath volatiles
(allyl methyl disulfide,

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.800
diallyl disulfide,
allyl mercaptan)

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.080
were significantly reduced
by parsley, spinach, mint,

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.960
raw and microwaved apple,
soft drink, green tea,

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.040
and lemon juice treatments

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.280
in comparison to water
(the control)

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:12.120
but were not reduced
by chlorophyll

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:13.960
and whey protein treatments.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:15.880
And perhaps
the polyphenol phytonutrients

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:18.240
were the active ingredient
in green tea.

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:20.920
With consumption
of full-flavor garlic,

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:23.640
it is not yet possible
to completely avoid

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:26.600
malodorous breath associated
with garlic consumption,

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.320
but there are some chasers

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:46.720
that may help you
bring it down a notch.

